From f5bfdb3475448c12044b254be8e32f2ba2fc8014 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Shammah Chancellor <shammah.chancellor@gmail.com>
Date: Sun, 16 May 2021 09:38:01 -0700
Subject: [PATCH] Implement raw encoding and decoding on XAddress format (#172)

This is the first commit required to implement parsing XAddress
formats. The basic idea is that addresses are composed of 4 parts:

1. token prefix (all lowercase word characters)
2. network byte (capital word character)
3. base58 encoded payload
4. base58 encoded 4-byte weak sha256d hash of (1)|| (2) || (3)

A follow up commit will implement processing into a `CTxDestination`
to support use in the rest of the node.

Rebase provenance: this historical change was adapted onto the pinned
Bitcoin ABC base. Source diff is the recorded Lotus V1 replay commit below.

Historical-source-commit: 6ef9ac191fcd170bb0f9417e5f5b6c590163fd6f
Recorded-replay-commit: bca3dd7f87ad11ac3a6bc1aeecf6045fe5be2ee0

